BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each had a sacred w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ell, but the wells held a secret: water poured into the First Well would flow underground an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    d emerge tripled from the Second Well.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  The First Village discovered this magic but faced a dilemma. To send water meant their own wel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    l would run lower. Yet the Second Village, receiving the tripled blessing, could choose to r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    eturn water-or keep it all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  At first, the First Village sent nothing, fearing betrayal. Both suffered through drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  Then a brave elder poured one bucket into the well. Three buckets emerged in the Second Villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    e. Grateful, they returned two buckets through the underground channels. The First Village r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ejoiced-they had sent one bucket but received two in return!) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  Trust grew like roots intertwining beneath the earth. The First Village sent more; the Second ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    Village returned generously. Both wells overflowed with abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  The villages learned that prosperity flows not from hoarding, but from the courage to give and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (     the honor to reciprocate. The magic multiplies what is shared, but only wisdom and fairness) Tj ET
