BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (        ed well, but the wells held a secret: water poured into the First Well would flow underg) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (        round and emerge tripled from the Second Well.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      The First Village discovered this magic but faced a dilemma. To send water meant their own) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (         well would run lower. Yet the Second Village, receiving the tripled blessing, could cho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (        ose to return water-or keep it all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      At first, the First Village sent nothing, fearing betrayal. Both suffered through drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      Then a brave elder poured one bucket into the well. Three buckets emerged in the Second Vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        llage. Grateful, they returned two buckets through the underground channels. The First V) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        illage rejoiced-they had sent one bucket but received two in return!) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      Trust grew like roots intertwining beneath the earth. The First Village sent more; the Sec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        ond Village returned generously. Both wells overflowed with abundance.) Tj ET
