BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from the Sacred Mountain - the River of Giving and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (         River of Receiving. Each was ruled by a guardian spirit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The Guardian of Giving possessed five silver coins each dawn. When she cast her coins into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (         the waters, they multiplied threefold by the time they reached the Guardian of Receivin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        g's domain. But the Guardian of Receiving held the power to decide: keep all the coins, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        or return some upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      For many seasons, fear ruled both guardians. The Giver held tight to her coins, sending no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        thing. The Receiver, when given anything, returned nothing. Both remained poor, and the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        land withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      Then came a great drought. In desperation, the Guardian of Giving released all five coins,) Tj ET
